    "body": "## Problem\r\n\r\nWith concealed text and `noinsert` or `noselect`, popup placement can apply conceal correction twice or use an offset measured at the real cursor rather than the completion start.\r\n\r\nFound while testing neovim/neovim#40897, but also reproduced on upstream master without that PR.\r\n\r\n## Solution\r\n\r\nCompute the completion-start column locally, using rendered-grid metadata for conceal without moving the real cursor or overwriting its cached column.\r\n\r\nKeep tab padding after concealed text mapped to its source column, and restore conceal-correct cursor state before `CompleteChanged` when returning from completion previews.\r\n\r\nExtend builtin/multigrid coverage for menu placement and cursor state, plus mouse coverage for tab padding.\r\n\r\n## Performance\r\n\r\nCompared the PR revision with its upstream merge base (`e7cd0e4375`) using optimized MSVC builds on Windows/i9-14900KF. The table reports medians of per-run average timings for warmed workloads, including editor redraw/UI flush. All times are in microseconds (`us`); lower is better.\r\n\r\n| Scenario                                    | Upstream (us) | This PR (us) |\r\n| ------------------------------------------- | ------------: | -----------: |\r\n| Ordinary completion, noinsert               |         22.54 |        22.56 |\r\n| Ordinary completion, auto-insert            |         31.99 |        31.92 |\r\n| Short concealed completion, noinsert        |         29.64 |        21.92 |\r\n| Short concealed completion, noselect        |         31.13 |        22.49 |\r\n| Concealed wrapped line, 80×24               |        231.43 |        38.63 |\r\n| Concealed wrapped line, 160×60              |      1,033.72 |       110.56 |\r\n| Concealed wrapped line, 400×120 stress case |      5,490.66 |       520.00 |\r\n| Visible regular preview                     |         89.89 |        87.25 |\r\n| Visible popup info                          |         59.07 |        53.61 |\r\n| Hidden popup info                           |         40.13 |        49.90 |\r\n| Forced redraw, plain text, 160×60           |        607.70 |       647.68 |\r\n| Forced redraw, concealed tabs, 160×60       |        461.46 |       485.41 |\r\n\r\nOrdinary completion was approximately unchanged. Concealed completion improved substantially, while hidden-info updates and forced redraws incurred additional cost.\r\n\r\nA separate external-UI microbenchmark isolated the grid lookup against a control that retained virtual-column preparation but returned a fixed, known-correct anchor. With the virtual-column cache valid, median added lookup costs were below 0.1us for 21 cells, approximately 3.1us for 7,701 cells, and 16.4us for 43,221 cells. These are component costs, not whole-PR deltas against upstream.\r\n\r\nThese synthetic measurements exclude frontend painting. The upstream baseline also has known positioning/callback errors in some conceal cases, so the timings do not imply identical correctness.\r\n",
