            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks. AI findings:\r\n\r\n1. Caret misplaced after the cmdline popupmenu (`popupmenu.c:315`)\r\n   - The new `w_wcol` invalidation also runs for the cmdline pum (`wildoptions=pum`, the default), where `cursor_col` comes from `cmd_startcol` and never reads `curwin->w_wcol`.\r\n   - It overwrites the conceal-corrected `w_wcol` from `win_line()` with the unconcealed value, keeps `VALID_WCOL` set, and nothing redraws the cursor line.\r\n   - Repro: in a help buffer (`cole=2 cocu=nc`), put the cursor after a concealed `|tag|`, then type `:h foo<Tab>` and `<Esc>`. The caret is drawn 2+ cells to the right of its real position until the cursor moves. `:popup` run from that\r\ncmdline is misplaced the same way.\r\n2. `w_wcol` is wrong right after `pum_display()` returns (`popupmenu.c:317`)\r\n   - In the noinsert/noselect case, `curwin->w_wcol` holds the unconcealed column with `VALID_WCOL` set until the `redrawWinline()` queued by `ins_compl_show_pum()` is drawn.\r\n   - A `CompleteChanged` autocmd that calls `wincol()` gets the unconcealed column; before this PR it got the corrected one.\r\n3. Not introduced here, but not fixed either: `w_wcol_conceal_off` is measured at the wrong column (`popupmenu.c:339`)\r\n   - `win_line()` measures the offset at the real cursor, but it is subtracted from the `w_wcol` computed for `compl_col`.\r\n   - Repro: `setline(1, 'foo bar xxx')` with `xxx` concealed, `cocu=nvic`, `completeopt=menuone,noinsert`. Press `A`, then `complete(5, ['barbaz'])`. The menu anchors at column 1 instead of column 4.\r\n   - An omnifunc/LSP start column before concealed text, or a wrapped row between `compl_col` and the cursor, hits the same mismatch.\r\n\r\n### Suggested approach\r\n\r\nMutating curwin's shared cursor cache causes 1 and 2, and 3 is still there. The root problem is that `w_wcol` has two writers that mean different things: `validate_cursor_col()` writes the unconcealed column, `win_line()` the concealed\r\none. Options:\r\n\r\n- Compute the unconcealed anchor into a local (factor the virtcol → wcol math out of `validate_cursor_col()` into a pure helper), without touching `curwin->w_wcol` or `w_valid`.\r\n- Or have `win_line()` record which column the offset was measured at, and apply the offset only when that column is `compl_col`.\r\n\r\nAt minimum: compute `curwin->w_p_cole > 0 && conceal_cursor_line(curwin)` once, and move the invalidation into the insert-mode branch next to the subtraction. That removes 1.\r\n\r\n### Tests\r\n\r\n- The test only checks the ext_popupmenu anchor. It doesn't check the grid or caret, the cmdline pum, or concealed text between `compl_col` and the cursor, so it can't catch any of the above.\r\n- Instead of a new `it()`, add noinsert/noselect iterations to the existing conceal tests (\"position with fully concealed text\" and its replacement-char/rightleft/wrap siblings). That also covers the builtin and multigrid pum.\r\n\r\n### Nits\r\n\r\n- Two comments in the function now explain `w_wcol` vs conceal and contradict each other. Document in `buffer_defs.h` (on `w_wcol` / `w_wcol_conceal_off`) that `win_line()` overwrites `w_wcol` with a conceal-corrected value, and drop the\r\ninline explanations.\r\n- `command('set completeopt=' .. cot)` → `command(('set completeopt=%s'):format(cot))`\r\n- `exec_lua(function() vim.fn.complete(vim.fn.col('.'), {...}) end)` → `fn.complete(fn.col('.'), { 'foobar', 'foobaz' })`\r\n",
