            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "The improvement to concealed completion comes from avoiding unnecessary redraws.\r\n\r\nPreviously, `ins_compl_show_pum()` temporarily moved the real cursor to the completion start and used its shared column cache to position the menu. After restoring the cursor, it queued a cursor-line redraw whenever conceal was active to repair the cached position -- even when `noinsert` or `noselect` left the text unchanged.\r\n\r\nThe PR calculates the anchor locally using the existing rendered-column metadata. It doesn't disturb the real cursor's cache, so ordinary menu updates no longer need that repair redraw.\r\n\r\nFor a long logical line, the old redraw could process many wrapped rows, including syntax and highlighting work. Reading the existing grid is much cheaper. That explains the large improvement in the measured 160×60 case: 1.03ms to 0.11ms.\r\n\r\nIt also fixes incorrect placement caused by double-applying conceal correction or using an offset measured at the wrong position. It does not make every rendering path faster: preview restoration and the renderer's additional metadata work account for the trade-offs reported in the table.",
